WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:06.450
Now let's move on to working with the translation itself.

2
00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:15.770
In review, we can see that this talk is already assigned to me:

3
00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:22.090
"Shri Vishnumaya Puja". We click – if we chose to work through

4
00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:25.810
"View translation", we click this button.

5
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:32.560
Here we see that there is a title, and we can

6
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.280
choose the video version.

7
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:41.880
Because this talk, this material, has two videos – the full

8
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:47.820
protocol, an hour and 37 minutes, or the Talk, 43

9
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.480
minutes. 44, sorry.

10
00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:56.660
And we have two modes – "Markers" or "Edit".

11
00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.270
We choose whichever suits us.

12
00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:06.300
Markers only let us make notes, roughly speaking, for ourselves,

13
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.860
saying that something here needs fixing, something needs work.

14
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.900
"Edit", on the other hand, lets us work with the subtitles directly,

15
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:16.950
and edit them.

16
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:22.620
So how does it work? We start playback,

17
00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:31.450
and when there is a subtitle we need to fix – we've spotted it –

18
00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:35.880
we click the "Edit" button.

19
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:42.300
So this viewing mode assumes that we

20
00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:46.910
have the video as the main source of picture and sound.

21
00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:50.430
We listen and translate it in our heads as we go.

22
00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:57.470
We read the translation, compare, and if we see

23
00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:04.420
some inaccuracy, we click "Edit" and fix it, for example, an extra

24
00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:05.420
full stop.

25
00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:13.130
Everything is designed for convenience, for automation,

26
00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.030
in the sense

27
00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:23.740
that during playback, if we need to edit something, we

28
00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:27.140
click a single "Edit" button – and the video pauses automatically.

29
00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.760
And the cursor is automatically here, in the edit field.

30
00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.820
We make the correction,

31
00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.840
press Enter – the video keeps playing.

32
00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:45.370
Again we see something to edit, click, make the correction again, press Enter –

33
00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:47.830
and it carries on.

34
00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:52.620
So that's how this mode works.

35
00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:58.210
And if we then want to show it full screen,

36
00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:04.410
for example, if we want to show this edited version of ours without the dots, there is

37
00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:10.760
a full-screen button, and that way we can already put it

38
00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.800
on air, if needed,

39
00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:19.600
without waiting for any changes to be published – these are our local changes.

40
00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.520
It may also be a little more comfortable in the "Dark" theme.

41
00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:31.480
That's a matter of taste. In the dark one, there will be darker

42
00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.580
sides here, as you prefer.

43
00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:35.900
And

44
00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:43.470
you can also play the original subtitles, to compare them,

45
00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:49.810
reading two sources. And this way you may even see that there are inaccuracies in

46
00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.050
the original subtitles.

47
00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:56.890
If there is an inaccuracy in the original subtitles, please also note it down

48
00:03:56.890 --> 00:04:03.510
somewhere, and it will be possible – feedback on the original English subtitles –

49
00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.510
to pass it on as well.

50
00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:13.010
The only thing is, the system here has no other place to write something. But,

51
00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:16.010
in general, please make a note for yourself.

52
00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:21.550
Or rather, here's how: for example, if you've noticed it, you can add a marker in markers,

53
00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.390
saying that here

54
00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.580
the English

55
00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:33.060
subtitles are inaccurate. For example,

56
00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:35.590
the word

57
00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.250
such-and-such

58
00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:43.770
needs replacing.

59
00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.280
Needs replacing.

60
00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:55.480
Say we've done that, and now let's look at these two kinds of changes.

61
00:04:56.060 --> 00:05:02.450
One is markers, our wish. The other is edits. Here we

62
00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:09.140
removed two commas. How can we pass these changes on from this page?

63
00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:15.040
Let's go to the markers first. This is our text message saying

64
00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.180
that something needs fixing.

65
00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.880
There are two buttons – "Copy all" and "Create issue".

66
00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.080
If you click "Copy all",

67
00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:31.440
it goes to the clipboard, and you can paste it with Ctrl+V somewhere later, send it on Telegram,

68
00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.300
however you like. Yes, just text.

69
00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:42.960
If you click "Create issue", a new tab opens where

70
00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:49.180
it will say that at such-and-such a point in time

71
00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:52.040
of such-and-such a talk

72
00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:56.810
there is such-and-such an issue. Let's try it and create one.

73
00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.970
We just click the green button.

74
00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:04.450
And here we have: such-and-such subtitle, such-and-such transcript, and this comment.

75
00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:08.090
Here the English subtitles are inaccurate, the word such-and-such needs replacing.

76
00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:13.660
Clearly, this is just a message.

77
00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:21.040
It refers to the Ukrainian subtitles, but if it's about the English translation,

78
00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:23.320
someone still has to work through it later anyway.

79
00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:31.830
So there are no final proposals from you here.

80
00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.710
It's just a comment, right?

81
00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.920
Whereas when we work in edit mode,

82
00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:45.740
these changes are already proposed as the final result, or rather, they can be proposed as

83
00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:50.600
final. We can click the same "Create issue" – it will be similar to what we

84
00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.820
created, just comments.

85
00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:58.560
Or we can click the green "Open in GitHub Editor" button.

86
00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.990
Let's click it and see what it tells us.

87
00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:03.690
"Subtitles copied".

88
00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:10.370
Click "Open GitHub", in the editor select all (Ctrl+A), paste (Ctrl+V).

89
00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:11.650
Let's try that.

90
00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.410
GitHub is open.

91
00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:21.970
We put the cursor inside this big field,

92
00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:26.320
press Ctrl+A, that is, select all,

93
00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:34.250
"Select All", and you can also press Ctrl+V or "Paste" –

94
00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:35.250
paste it.

95
00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:43.600
After that, just as when we added new material, we click

96
00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:47.180
green button 1, green button 2

97
00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:50.270
and the green button.

98
00:07:55.320 --> 00:08:00.600
With that, our proposed change is ready.

99
00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:05.800
On the "Files changed" tab we can see these proposals.

100
00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:11.700
In our case you can see that two dots were removed, and here too.

101
00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:16.340
Here some extra empty line at the end was removed.

102
00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:22.450
But as you can see, a "Refresh" button has appeared here too. What does that mean?

103
00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:28.790
That when we created this proposal, the automation synced our changes to

104
00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:31.150
some other place as well. Let's take a fresh look.

105
00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:36.840
We see that these changes also reached the transcript,

106
00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.950
not only the subtitles, but the transcript too.

107
00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:48.820
Actually, once you have submitted this change proposal,

108
00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:55.760
your work is done at that point; you can pass on this link,

109
00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:01.870
or send it to me, and I'll take a look, a second pair of eyes, so to speak,

110
00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:05.610
and accept these changes.

111
00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:11.990
I'll check that all the procedures here have passed and run.

112
00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:18.410
Here not all the syncs passed; the second subtitles did not sync.

113
00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.150
I'll look into it,

114
00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:24.630
fix it so they sync, and accept them.

115
00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:31.970
In time, if it is always all green and nobody needs to look at anything by hand

116
00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:32.970
or fix anything,

117
00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:34.650
then

118
00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:42.540
you won't need to send me anything, and you'll click this green one yourselves once

119
00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:43.540
more.

120
00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:50.230
In effect, this is what it looks like: you have a pull request

121
00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:52.840
created.

122
00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:59.000
You see the final version of the changes you submitted.

123
00:10:01.090 --> 00:10:05.290
As a matter of good practice, someone else should check that no

124
00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:09.590
mistakes were made and no automation failed,

125
00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:17.840
and after that the changes are accepted into the system and appear on the portal.

126
00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:26.230
Overall, that is the procedure for working with the preview page and

127
00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:29.550
submitting the finished material from it.
